// 2540
[dbrow_2540]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,You have many skills you can train.<br>The more you practice a skill, the better it gets.<br><br>Higher skill levels unlock new activities: equipment to craft, locations to explore, quests to complete, and much more.
data=col5,interface_1466:com_0
data=col6,-1
data=col7,3
data=col15,"staticons_high_res_clean,0"

// 2541
[dbrow_2541]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Perform actions associated with a skill to earn experience points (XP) in that skill.<br>Earn enough XP, and you'll gain a level in that skill.
data=col5,interface_1466:com_0
data=col6,-1
data=col7,3
data=col15,"staticons_high_res_clean,0"
data=col16,"aif_money_xp_icons,0"
data=col17,"aif_level_up_text_language_gold,3"

// 2542
[dbrow_2542]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Most skills start at level 1, and you unlock all their benefits by leveling the skill to 99.<br>(Some skills have unlocks up to level 120.)
data=col5,interface_1466:com_0
data=col6,-1
data=col7,3

// 2543
[dbrow_2543]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,The bottom number next to a skill icon is your base level in that skill (un-modified by buffs or debuffs). It is used for most requirement checks.
data=col5,interface_1466:com_0
data=col6,-1
data=col7,3
data=col20,interface_1466:com_5,2

// 2544
[dbrow_2544]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,The top number is your modified skill level (temporarily boosted or drained by skill buffs and debuffs - such as potions or spells). It is used for most skill checks.
data=col5,interface_1466:com_0
data=col6,-1
data=col7,3
data=col20,interface_1466:com_4,2

// 2545
[dbrow_2545]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Achieve 99 in all your skills to earn the coveted Max Cape!
data=col5,interface_1466:com_0
data=col6,-1
data=col7,3
data=col15,aif_pttp_voting_banner_master_skillcapes

// 2546
[dbrow_2546]
table=dbtable_71

// 2547
[dbrow_2547]
table=dbtable_72
data=col3,Most of your skills require some kind of tool. For example, woodcutting requires a hatchet, and mining requires a pickaxe.<br><br>You start with a bronze hatchet, pickaxe and some other basic tools on your toolbelt. Items on your toolbelt are protected if you die.
data=col5,interface_1464:com_23
data=col6,4
data=col7,1
data=col19,obj_1265
data=col20,interface_1464:com_23,4

