// 3334
[dbrow_3334]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,26
data=col1,2
data=col3,Ikovian Tragedy
data=col4,70
data=col6,Little is known about the Temple of Ikov, given how little of it still stands in the current age.
data=col7,The research team has uncovered that the Ikovians were early human followers of Armadyl, and that the temple stands as a memorial to some sort of massacre of the Ikovians in the early Third Age.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49656,1

// 3335
[dbrow_3335]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,27
data=col1,2
data=col3,Deer-ly Departed
data=col4,81
data=col6,Stormguard's landing pad is littered with megaliths. We're not sure yet of their significance, but they are reminiscent of other cultures' so-called 'deer stones'.
data=col7,Aviansie typically fight along with a partner - a spouse or close friend. If one of a coupling dies, the survivor typically joins the keshik Dayguard or Nightguard and it becomes their new family. These memorial stones remember their lost partners.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49632,1

// 3336
[dbrow_3336]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,28
data=col1,2
data=col3,The Aetherium Giant
data=col4,98
data=col6,This area of Stormguard is littered with remnants of destroyed golems, most notable of which is the arm of a giant war golem. There's also a wealth of strange and wonderful devices and advanced weaponry.
data=col7,The Stormguard Citadel appears to have been some sort of secret testing facility, not solely for weapons, but no doubt that during the God Wars weapon development was a primary concern.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49644,1

// 3337
[dbrow_3337]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,29
data=col1,2
data=col3,Night and Day
data=col4,95
data=col6,The outer parts of what remains of Stormguard seems to contain the ruins of old guard towers.
data=col7,The Dayguard and Nightguard keshik warriors were seemingly stationed at Stormguard in part to protect its more scientific inhabitants, should the external lightning cloud shielding fail, but also to test out various experimental weapons.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49658,1

// 3338
[dbrow_3338]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,30
data=col1,2
data=col3,Howling Man
data=col4,118
data=col6,An alchemical laboratory sits floating higher than other remaining sections of Stormguard, filled with all kinds of arcane and mystical devices we don't understand.
data=col7,According to various blueprints and notebooks, this laboratory was home to an aviansie alchemist who went by the codename 'Howl' (likely to protect his true identity). His works are far ahead of other technology we have dug up from the Third Age, and his ideas well ahead of their time.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49638,1

// 3339
[dbrow_3339]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,31
data=col1,2
data=col3,Back to the Drawing Board
data=col4,95
data=col6,A drafting table sits within Stormguard's workshop, upon which sit many blueprints, notes and books all written in an unusual cipher.
data=col7,The research team have cracked Howl's cipher! We can now understand this eccentric alchemist's designs and start trying to build some of them...
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49664,1
data=col15,obj_50108,50

// 3340
[dbrow_3340]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,153
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_wingsuit_v1
data=col3,This set of artificial wings was originally created as a prosphetic for injured aviansie, but work just as well at giving flight to the flightless, albeit only nearby Stormguard Citadel's gravitational core.
data=col4,76
data=col5,obj_50119
data=col6,obj_50120
data=col7,0
data=col8,0

