// 3382
[dbrow_3382]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,32
data=col1,2
data=col3,Melting Point
data=col4,83
data=col6,The underground arena we've uncovered is still in a quite well-preserved condition.
data=col7,Only goblin remains have been discovered within the Warforge's Crucible arena. Other artefacts suggest this arena was used to teach goblin warfare, but clearly, it wasn't exactly safe, and only the fittest goblins survived.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49732,1

// 3383
[dbrow_3383]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,34
data=col1,2
data=col3,Too Many Bones
data=col4,100
data=col6,There are a series of barricaded chambers south of the luminescent underground river, with lots of scattered weapons.
data=col7,The research team suspects the chambers in the south of the Warforge consist of sleeping areas - a cramped dormitory for most of the goblins that lived here, a 'luxury' boudoir for the current tournament champion, and a series of pens for various animals and their keepers.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49686,1

// 3384
[dbrow_3384]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,33
data=col1,2
data=col3,Northside
data=col4,97
data=col6,The chambers in the northern part of these goblin tunnels are littered with barricades and signs of a skirmish.
data=col7,The chambers north of the river consist of an armoury, a sparring area and a ritual area/shrine to the 'Big High War God', whom we know to be Bandos. There is evidence that there was a great deal of fighting in these tunnels.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49692,1

// 3385
[dbrow_3385]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,35
data=col1,2
data=col3,Dwarven Forge
data=col4,97
data=col6,The source of heat from beneath the Crucible turns out to be a dwarven forge. What is a dwarven forge doing hidden within a Bandosian stronghold?
data=col7,The research team has discovered that the forge beneath the Crucible is of imcando construction! Evidence points to a kidnapped imcando dwarf being taken as a prisoner and forced to smith weapons for the Warforge, among other things.
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49720,1

// 3386
[dbrow_3386]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,36
data=col1,2
data=col3,Big High War Chest
data=col4,119
data=col6,Archaeologists have uncovered a hidden area behind Bandos's throne, containing a variety of weapons.
data=col7,It seems that Bandos left this place in something of a hurry, being that he left behind a number of Kal-i-kra artefacts. Our researchers suggest the Kal-i-kra were a tribe from which Bandos originated before his ascension. Some rare finds here, indeed!
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49726,1

// 3387
[dbrow_3387]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,37
data=col1,2
data=col3,Power Behind the Throne
data=col4,100
data=col6,The mechanism that was discovered in the side of Bandos's throne likely unlocks something nearby. Perhaps the research team can figure out how it works.
data=col7,The research team believe that placing a 'Forged in War' Kyzaj sculpture into the recess on the side of Bandos's throne will unlock something nearby...
data=col8,4000
data=col15,obj_49728,1

